A result field is mapped onto an item field with the conversion that field's widget calls for (`widgetToTargetType`, now in `@volto-hydra/helpers/mappingConversions.js`: the one derivation converting a block, pulling from a linked page and storing a listing's mapping all use), unless its value needs another (a list into text is joined). One rule says which fit: text into text, textarea or slate; the address into a link or text; an image into an image or link field as `image_link`, its scales kept; a date into a date or text; a list into a list or text; a yes/no into a yes/no. The field-mapping widget offers each source only the fields it fits, and stores it with that conversion (see the breaking change on stored mappings). The editor refuses to load a config whose mappings break the rule or name a source type it can't convert, along with a source or destination the schemas don't have, a mapping onto an id, type or template key (a region's idField included), or a block field named `@id` at any depth. The content check applies the rule to every listing's stored mapping, and no longer excuses an `href` the item type doesn't declare.
